  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-250000993</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seeding local cultures</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project addresses the issue of malnutrition exacerbated by water scarcity by implementing Integrated Land Use Design (ILUD) approaches into the management of school grounds at 3 primary, 2 secondary, and 2 tertiary institutions while promoting the inclusion of permaculture and agroforestry into the national curriculum of Zimbabwe. Activities thus involve students, teachers and school managers (learning and implementing new knowledge), teaching colleges, and the Ministry of Education (working to include permaculture into the national curriculum more broadly). The anticipated long-term outcomes include reduced land degradation, improved ecosystem services and food security and health at the schools and the home communities of teachers and learners.</narrative>
  </description>
